# Collection tags and the works state on the item lists: TAG= (whole
# tags, A-Z folded, every one listed) and WORKS= (any of Y I N ?) on ITEM
# LIST, ITEM FIND and REPORT ITEMS, with the other filters and ALL=1;
# their refusals; REPORT ITEMS' WORKS column; and ITEM TAGS, the tags in
# use, each once in its first spelling, A-Z folded, page by page.
#
# Fixture (TAGS as given; WORKS):
#   1 SYS  IBM 5150         RM  Retro                      Y
#   2 CARD 3Com 3C509       SH  "retro, network"           y
#   3 CARD Intel Gigabit    SH  network,modern             (?)
#   4 CARD Acme Metro       RM  metro,retro2               N
#   5 DRV  Seagate ST-225   --  "RETRO isa Retro"          I
#   6 CBL  Acme Cable       --  (none)                     ?
# Shelf SH stands in room RM; item 2 is on loan.

> HELLO CONSOLE
< +OK
> LOGIN ADMIN admin
< +OK LEVEL=3 MUSTCHG=1
> PASSWD admin secret1
< +OK
> LOC ADD LOC_NAME=Room LTYPE=ROOM LOC_CODE=RM
< +OK ID=1
> LOC ADD LOC_NAME=Shelf LTYPE=SHELF LOC_CODE=SH PARENT_ID=RM
< +OK ID=2
> ITEM ADD CATEGORY=SYS MFR=IBM MODEL=5150 LOC_ID=RM TAGS=Retro WORKS=Y
< +OK ID=1
> ITEM ADD CATEGORY=CARD MFR=3Com MODEL=3C509 LOC_ID=SH TAGS="retro, network" WORKS=y
< +OK ID=2
> ITEM ADD CATEGORY=CARD MFR=Intel MODEL=Gigabit LOC_ID=SH TAGS=network,modern
< +OK ID=3
> ITEM ADD CATEGORY=CARD MFR=Acme MODEL=Metro LOC_ID=RM TAGS=metro,retro2 WORKS=N
< +OK ID=4
> ITEM ADD CATEGORY=DRV MFR=Seagate MODEL=ST-225 TAGS="RETRO isa Retro" WORKS=I
< +OK ID=5
> ITEM ADD CATEGORY=CBL MFR=Acme MODEL=Cable WORKS=?
< +OK ID=6
> LOAN OUT 2 HOLDER=Al DUE=20261231
< +OK ID=1

# The stored tags: single commas, a repeat left out, the first spelling.
> ITEM LIST FIELDS=ITEM_ID,TAGS,WORKS
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID TAGS WORKS
< R 1 Retro Y
< R 2 retro,network Y
< R 3 network,modern ?
< R 4 metro,retro2 N
< R 5 RETRO,isa I
< R 6 "" ?
< .

# TAG= keeps the items carrying every tag listed, whole and A-Z folded:
# metro and retro2 are not retro.  An empty TAG= filters nothing.
> ITEM LIST TAG=retro FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 1
< R 2
< R 5
< .
> item list tag=RETRO,Network fields=item_id
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 2
< .
> ITEM LIST TAG="network  retro" FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 2
< .
> ITEM LIST TAG=retro2 FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 4
< .
> ITEM LIST TAG=retro,isa,modern FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< .
> ITEM LIST TAG= FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 1
< R 2
< R 3
< R 4
< R 5
< R 6
< .

# Beside CAT=, AVAIL= and LOC=; ITEM FIND's text still matches TAGS as
# a substring, TAG= only whole tags.
> ITEM LIST CAT=card TAG=network AVAIL=1 FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 3
< .
> ITEM LIST CAT=CARD TAG=network AVAIL=0 FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 2
< .
> ITEM LIST LOC=SH TAG=retro FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 2
< .
> ITEM FIND net FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 2
< R 3
< .
> ITEM FIND net TAG=retro FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 2
< .
> ITEM FIND net TAG=net FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< .

# ALL=1: the tree below LOC=, in tree order, with both filters.
> ITEM LIST LOC=RM ALL=1 TAG=retro FIELDS=ITEM_ID,LOC_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID LOC_ID
< R 1 1
< R 2 2
< .
> ITEM FIND giga LOC=RM ALL=1 TAG=network WORKS=? FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 3
< .

> ITEM LIST LOC=RM ALL=1 WORKS=Y FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 1
< R 2
< .

# WORKS=: one letter or several, any case; Y?I leaves out only the
# items known not to work.
> ITEM LIST WORKS=Y FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 1
< R 2
< .
> ITEM LIST WORKS=y?i FIELDS=ITEM_ID,WORKS
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID WORKS
< R 1 Y
< R 2 Y
< R 3 ?
< R 5 I
< R 6 ?
< .
> ITEM LIST WORKS=N FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 4
< .
> ITEM LIST WORKS=YNI? FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 1
< R 2
< R 3
< R 4
< R 5
< R 6
< .
> ITEM FIND acme WORKS=? FIELDS=ITEM_ID
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID
< R 6
< .

# Refused filters: another letter, a repeat, more than four letters; a
# TAG= over 25 characters, with a word that is no tag, or of
# separators only.
> ITEM LIST WORKS=X
< -ERR 102 works must be Y, N, I or ? FIELD=WORKS
> ITEM LIST WORKS=YNy
< -ERR 102 works must be Y, N, I or ? FIELD=WORKS
> ITEM LIST WORKS=YNI?Y
< -ERR 102 works must be Y, N, I or ? FIELD=WORKS
> ITEM FIND ibm WORKS=Q
< -ERR 102 works must be Y, N, I or ? FIELD=WORKS
> REPORT ITEMS WORKS=YN?Z
< -ERR 102 works must be Y, N, I or ? FIELD=WORKS
> ITEM LIST TAG=abcdefghijkl,abcdefghijklm
< -ERR 102 filter value too long FIELD=TAG
> ITEM LIST TAG=abcdefghijkl,abcdefghijkl
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID CATEGORY MFR MODEL WORKS QTY AVAIL LOC_ID LOC_NAME STATUS
< .
> ITEM LIST TAG=abcdefghijklm
< -ERR 102 each tag 1-12 of A-Z a-z 0-9 - _ . / + FIELD=TAG
> ITEM LIST TAG=retro*
< -ERR 102 each tag 1-12 of A-Z a-z 0-9 - _ . / + FIELD=TAG
> ITEM FIND ibm TAG=",, ,"
< -ERR 102 each tag 1-12 of A-Z a-z 0-9 - _ . / + FIELD=TAG
> ITEM LIST LOC=RM ALL=1 TAG=a:b
< -ERR 102 each tag 1-12 of A-Z a-z 0-9 - _ . / + FIELD=TAG

# The default columns show WORKS; REPORT ITEMS has COND and WORKS.
> ITEM LIST TAG=retro WORKS=Y
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID CATEGORY MFR MODEL WORKS QTY AVAIL LOC_ID LOC_NAME STATUS
< R 1 SYS IBM 5150 Y 1 Y 1 Room A
< R 2 CARD 3Com 3C509 Y 1 L 2 Shelf A
< .
> REPORT ITEMS TAG=retro WORKS=Y
< +DATA
< F ITEM_ID CATEGORY MFR MODEL SERIALNO COND WORKS QTY LOC_ID LOC_NAME STATUS ACQ_DATE ACQ_PRICE CUR_VALUE
< R 1 SYS IBM 5150 "" "" Y 1 1 Room A "" "" ""
< R 2 CARD 3Com 3C509 "" "" Y 1 2 Shelf A "" "" ""
< .

# ITEM TAGS: every tag once, A-Z folded, in its first spelling, in A-Z
# folded order; a page from a cursor starts afresh.
> ITEM TAGS
< +DATA
< F TAG
< R isa
< R metro
< R modern
< R network
< R Retro
< R retro2
< .
> item tags after=ITEMS::4
< +DATA
< F TAG
< R isa
< R RETRO
< .
> ITEM TAGS AFTER=ITEMS::5
< +DATA
< F TAG
< .
> ITEM TAGS AFTER=ITEMS::6
< +DATA
< F TAG
< .
> ITEM DEL 4
< +OK
> ITEM SET 3 STATUS=D
< +OK
> ITEM TAGS AFTER=ITEMS::2
< +DATA
< F TAG
< R isa
< R modern
< R network
< R RETRO
< .

# A page reads at most 200 records: its C line names the last one, and
# the next page goes on after it.
@REPEAT 200
> ITEM ADD CATEGORY=CBL
< +OK ID=206
> ITEM ADD CATEGORY=CBL TAGS=last
< +OK ID=207
> ITEM TAGS
< +DATA
< F TAG
< R isa
< R modern
< R network
< R Retro
< C ITEMS::C8
< .
> ITEM TAGS AFTER=ITEMS::C8
< +DATA
< F TAG
< R last
< .

# Its refusals: a bad cursor, a key, a word.
> ITEM TAGS AFTER=junk
< -ERR 204 bad cursor
> ITEM TAGS AFTER=ITEMS1:20:1
< -ERR 204 bad cursor
> ITEM TAGS PAGE=2
< -ERR 102 unexpected key FIELD=PAGE
> ITEM TAGS ALL
< -ERR 100 too many arguments
